   VVeerrssiioonnss
       POSIX message queues have been supported since Linux 2.6.6.  glibc sup‐
       port has been provided since glibc 2.3.4.

   KKeerrnneell ccoonnffiigguurraattiioonn
       Support  for  POSIX  message  queues  is  configurable  via  the   CCOONN‐‐
       FFIIGG__PPOOSSIIXX__MMQQUUEEUUEE  kernel  configuration option.  This option is enabled
       by default.

   PPeerrssiisstteennccee
       POSIX message queues have kernel persistence: if not removed by  mmqq__uunn‐‐
       lliinnkk(3), a message queue will exist until the system is shut down.

